# Paper II General Ability Test, Part B General Knowledge, Section E:
# geography of the Earth and of India (about 20 percent). Static facts only.
# Key written first.
ITEMS = [
    # ---------- Practice Test 1 ----------
    S(1, 2, "Landforms", "Fjords, the long, narrow, steep-sided sea inlets of Norway, were carved by:",
      ["Glaciers", "Rivers", "Wind", "Waves"],
      "Fjords are U-shaped valleys deepened by glaciers during the Ice Age and later flooded by the sea when the ice melted."),
    S(1, 2, "Rivers", "Where does the Mahanadi river rise?",
      ["Near Sihawa in Chhattisgarh", "At Amarkantak", "At Talakaveri", "Near Multai in Madhya Pradesh"],
      "The Mahanadi rises near Sihawa in Dhamtari district of Chhattisgarh and flows east through Odisha to the Bay of Bengal. The Narmada rises at Amarkantak, the Kaveri at Talakaveri and the Tapi near Multai."),
    S(1, 2, "Atmosphere", "In the troposphere, the air temperature usually:",
      ["Falls with height, by about 6.5 °C per kilometre", "Rises with height, by about 6.5 °C per kilometre", "Stays the same at every height", "Falls only above 50 km"],
      "Air is heated mainly from the ground below, so in the troposphere it gets colder with height, on average by about 6.5 °C per km (the normal lapse rate). That is why mountain tops are cold."),
    S(1, 2, "Climate", "The hot, dry, dusty wind that blows over north-west India and the Gangetic plains on summer afternoons is called:",
      ["Loo", "Mango shower", "Kalbaisakhi", "Western disturbance"],
      "The loo blows in May and June. Mango showers are pre-monsoon rains in Kerala and Karnataka, Kalbaisakhi is a storm in Bengal, and western disturbances bring winter rain to the north-west."),
    S(1, 2, "Landforms", "A crescent-shaped sand dune with its horns pointing downwind is called:",
      ["A barchan", "A delta", "A moraine", "A drumlin"],
      "Barchans form in deserts where the wind blows steadily from one direction and sand is limited. Moraines and drumlins are left by glaciers, and a delta is built by a river."),
    S(1, 2, "Indian geography", "The hills along India's border with Myanmar, including the Patkai, Naga and Mizo hills, are together called the:",
      ["Purvanchal", "Aravallis", "Satpuras", "Karakoram"],
      "The Purvanchal (eastern hills) are the eastern extension of the Himalaya, running along the India-Myanmar border. The Aravallis and Satpuras are in peninsular India and the Karakoram in the far north."),
    S(1, 2, "Earth", "The International Date Line roughly follows which line of longitude?",
      ["180°", "0°", "90° E", "82.5° E"],
      "The International Date Line runs mostly along the 180° meridian, bending to avoid land. 0° is the Prime Meridian at Greenwich and 82.5° E is India's standard meridian."),
    S(1, 2, "Oceans", "The Gulf Stream is:",
      ["A warm current in the North Atlantic Ocean", "A cold current off the coast of Peru", "A warm current in the Indian Ocean", "A cold current off the coast of Japan"],
      "The Gulf Stream carries warm water from the Gulf of Mexico across the North Atlantic, keeping north-western Europe milder than its latitude suggests. The cold current off Peru is the Humboldt (Peru) Current."),
    S(1, 1, "Earth", "The Arctic Circle lies at about which latitude?",
      ["66.5° N", "23.5° N", "45° N", "90° N"],
      "The Arctic Circle is at about 66.5° N, that is 90° minus the 23.5° tilt of the Earth's axis. 23.5° N is the Tropic of Cancer and 90° N the North Pole."),
    S(1, 2, "Indian geography", "Guru Shikhar, near Mount Abu, is the highest peak of:",
      ["The Aravalli Range", "The Andaman Islands", "The Nilgiri Hills", "The Satpura Range"],
      "Guru Shikhar (about 1,722 m) rises near Mount Abu in Rajasthan and is the highest point of the Aravallis. The Andamans rise to Saddle Peak, the Nilgiris to Doddabetta and the Satpuras to Dhupgarh."),
    # ---------- Practice Test 2 ----------
    S(2, 1, "Solar system", "The asteroid belt lies between the orbits of:",
      ["Mars and Jupiter", "Earth and Mars", "Jupiter and Saturn", "Venus and Earth"],
      "Most asteroids orbit the Sun between Mars and Jupiter. Ceres, the largest object there, is classed as a dwarf planet."),
    S(2, 2, "Rocks", "Marble is a metamorphic rock formed from:",
      ["Limestone", "Granite", "Sandstone", "Shale"],
      "Heat and pressure recrystallise limestone into marble. Sandstone becomes quartzite, shale becomes slate, and granite becomes gneiss."),
    S(2, 2, "Oceans", "Which ocean current is cold?",
      ["Labrador Current", "Gulf Stream", "Kuroshio Current", "Brazil Current"],
      "The Labrador Current brings cold Arctic water south past Newfoundland, where it meets the warm Gulf Stream and causes fog. The other three are warm currents."),
    S(2, 2, "Earth", "The Tropic of Capricorn passes through which of these countries?",
      ["Brazil", "India", "Egypt", "Mexico"],
      "The Tropic of Capricorn (about 23.5° S) crosses Brazil, Paraguay, Argentina, Chile, southern Africa, Madagascar and Australia. India, Egypt and Mexico are crossed by the Tropic of Cancer."),
    S(2, 2, "Climate", "Western disturbances, which bring winter rain and snow to north-west India, come from:",
      ["The Mediterranean region", "The Bay of Bengal", "The Arabian Sea in summer", "The Tibetan plateau"],
      "Western disturbances are low-pressure systems that start over the Mediterranean and travel east with the westerly jet stream. Their winter rain helps the rabi crop in Punjab and Haryana."),
    S(2, 2, "Indian geography", "Mount Saramati, the highest peak of Nagaland, lies on the border with:",
      ["Myanmar", "Bhutan", "China", "Bangladesh"],
      "Saramati (about 3,840 m) is in the Naga Hills on the India-Myanmar border."),
    S(2, 2, "Agriculture", "Shifting cultivation in north-east India, in which a patch of forest is cleared, farmed for a few years and then left, is called:",
      ["Jhum", "Terrace farming", "Plantation farming", "Ley farming"],
      "Jhum is slash-and-burn farming practised in the hills of the north-east. It is known by other names elsewhere, such as podu in Andhra Pradesh and Odisha."),
    S(2, 2, "Indian geography", "Long, flat-floored valleys between the Shiwaliks and the Lesser Himalaya, such as the one in which Dehradun stands, are called:",
      ["Duns", "Doabs", "Karewas", "Kayals"],
      "Duns (or doons) are longitudinal valleys between the Shiwalik range and the Lesser Himalaya; Dehradun and Patli Dun are examples. A doab is the land between two rivers, karewas are lake deposits in the Kashmir valley, and kayals are the backwaters of Kerala."),
    S(2, 1, "Earth", "Day and night are caused by:",
      ["The rotation of the Earth on its axis", "The revolution of the Earth around the Sun", "The tilt of the Earth's axis", "The movement of the Moon"],
      "The Earth turns on its axis once in about 24 hours, so each place faces the Sun and then turns away. Revolution and the tilt of the axis together cause the seasons."),
    S(2, 2, "Earth", "Most tsunamis are caused by:",
      ["Earthquakes under the sea floor", "Strong winds over the ocean", "The pull of the Moon at high tide", "Melting icebergs"],
      "A sudden movement of the sea floor in an undersea earthquake lifts a huge column of water, which spreads as a tsunami. The 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami began with an earthquake off Sumatra."),
    # ---------- Drill only ----------
    S(0, 2, "Earth", "On which dates are day and night roughly equal all over the world?",
      ["About 21 March and 23 September", "About 21 June and 22 December", "About 1 January and 1 July", "About 15 August and 26 January"],
      "These are the equinoxes, when the Sun is overhead at the equator. 21 June and 22 December are the solstices, the longest and shortest days in the northern hemisphere."),
    S(0, 2, "Indian geography", "The coastal plain between the Western Ghats and the Arabian Sea in Kerala is known as the:",
      ["Malabar coast", "Coromandel coast", "Northern Circars", "Konkan coast"],
      "The Malabar coast runs along Kerala and southern Karnataka, with lagoons called kayals. The Konkan coast is to its north, and the Coromandel coast and Northern Circars are on the east."),
]
